'''Warps''' are the ''{{w|Gacha game|gacha}}'' system in ''[[Honkai: Star Rail]]'' and the primary method to obtain [[Character]]s and [[Light Cone]]s.

The Warp system is unlocked during the {{Mission|A Moment of Peace|showChapter=0}}.

==Types==
* [[Departure Warp]]
* [[Stellar Warp]]
* [[Character Event Warp]]
* [[Light Cone Event Warp]]
* [[Character Collaboration Warp]]
* [[Light Cone Collaboration Warp]]

==Availability==
The [[Stellar Warp]] is always available and requires {{Item|Star Rail Pass|text=Star Rail Passes}}.

The [[Departure Warp]] is available indefinitely until all 50 Warps are made. It has a 20% discount using batch Warps, requiring only 40 Star Rail Passes to complete all 50 pulls. Within this limit, players are guaranteed to obtain one non-promotional 5{{Star}} character.

Limited-time Event Warps are split into two types: [[Character Event Warp]]s and [[Light Cone Event Warp]]s. As the name suggests, they are only available for a limited time and require {{Item|Star Rail Special Pass|text=Star Rail Special Passes}} instead of Star Rail Passes.

Character Event Warps have one promotional 5{{Star}} character and three featured 4{{Star}} characters. Light Cone Event Warps have one promotional 5{{Star}} Light Cone and three featured 4{{Star}} Light Cones. Both the promotional 5{{Star}} and featured 4{{Star}} items have an increased drop rate compared to the basic rates when the guarantees are factored in.

Players can buy either of the Passes for {{Item|Stellar Jade|x=160}} each from the Warp menu or through the [[Store]]. However, purchasing is optional, as Stellar Jade will be used in place of missing Passes when performing a Warp. Additionally, there are also in-game methods of obtaining Passes; see their respective pages for more information.

